e('**XDP** (eXpress Data Path) is the earliest hook: it runs in the driver\'s NAPI poll, on the raw DMA buffer, **before an skb is allocated**.','**Native XDP** (eXpress Data Path) runs early in a supporting driver\'s receive path, before the normal skb-based stack path. Generic XDP operates after skb allocation, and hardware offload runs elsewhere.','Modesdiffer.',xp)
e('A program that drops UDP traffic to port 9999:','This parsing fragment classifies untagged, unfragmented IPv4 UDP destination port 9999. It deliberately passes other formats, fragments and malformed lengths onward; it is not a complete firewall or fragment-reassembly policy. Supply Linux/BPF headers, a loader and license declaration:', 'Incompletefilterexplicit scope.',ver+ip)
